Video key-frame (TU0) byte parity: preset-7 cell closed
2026-09-26

Host: i265-class box (Intel i9-13900K), Linux x86_64, GCC 14.3.0.
Commands: tools/video_census_gate.sh (VCG_WRITE=1, VCG_JOBS=6), ~207 s,
540 cells (6 derf clips x 2 sizes x 3 qps x presets -1..13, 8 frames each,
key-frame-first verdict from tools/inter_byte_matrix.py).

Change under test: PD1 `test_split_partition` early-exit controls made
per-arm — `FunnelCfg::depth_early_exit` + `parent_cost_bias` stamped by
`encdec_arm::apply` (video arm: level 2 `early_exit_th` 900 at enc_mode >
ENC_M6, per `svt_aom_sig_deriv_enc_dec_default`; allintra: level 1 through
M7). Before: hardcoded `EE_SPLIT_TH=50`, `EE_EARLY_TH=1000`,
`PARENT_COST_BIAS=995` in depth_refine/walk.rs.

Pinned verdicts (tools/pins/video_census.tsv): 244 -> 260 IDENTICAL of 540.
TU0 cells: 16 -> 8. All 11 moved rows are preset 7, all improvements:

  fourpeople      128 q55 p7  TU0 -> IDENTICAL
  fourpeople      256 q40 p7  TU0 -> IDENTICAL
  fourpeople      256 q55 p7  TU0 -> IDENTICAL
  kristenandsara  256 q40 p7  TU0 -> IDENTICAL
  kristenandsara  256 q55 p7  TU0 -> IDENTICAL
  vidyo1          128 q55 p7  TU0 -> IDENTICAL
  vidyo1          256 q55 p7  TU0 -> IDENTICAL
  vidyo3          256 q55 p7  TU0 -> TU3   (key frame now identical; the
                                          TU3 divergence is inter, item (b))
  johnny          256 q40 p7  TU2 -> IDENTICAL
  vidyo4          128 q40 p7  TU6 -> IDENTICAL
  vidyo4          256 q40 p7  TU1 -> TU3

Remaining TU0 cells (all at presets 10..13, all qp 55, all 256x256):
vidyo1 p10; vidyo3 p10..13; kristenandsara p11..13 — a DIFFERENT defect
class: on vidyo3 p10 the leaf eval at mi(4,0) 16x16 over-prices rate by 724
vs C (37765 vs 37041, same dist/mode), which keeps the qp-scaled
`nsq_split_cost_th` gate from skipping the VERT shape C never tested —
resolved in the second landing below; evidence is in
PLAN-ORACLES-AND-CLEANUP.md 3.8.

Acceptance at this commit: cargo nextest --workspace --locked 2756/2756;
regression_spotcheck 147/147; video_key_matrix 75/75; output pins 6/6;
identity_full_8bit 1100/1100; real_video_inter_gate 24/24 (0 regressed);
video_selfcheck_gate 270/270; tools/precheck.sh OK.

Second landing, same session (tx_mode gate): video M10+ (and non-base
frames at M8/M9) use `frm_hdr->tx_mode = TX_MODE_LARGEST`, so C prices
zero tx-size bits in every `svt_aom_tx_size_bits` call (rd_cost.c:1755,
plus the depth-sweep compares at product_coding_loop.c:5380/5395). The
port's leaf-rate sites dropped the `tx_mode` check and over-priced every
leaf by one tx-size symbol (+366/+724 measured at mi(0,0)/(4,0) on vidyo3
256 q55 p10), which kept the qp-scaled `nsq_split_cost_th` gate from
skipping the VERT shape C never tested at mi(4,0). Fixed via
`FunnelFrame::tx_mode_select` gated into mds1/mds3/tx_depth/light rate
terms. Allintra is byte-neutral (SELECT unconditionally).

video_census_gate: 260 -> 284 IDENTICAL of 540; TU0 class now EMPTY (0
cells diverge at the key frame). 36 pins moved, all improvements, all at
p10..13 (e.g. vidyo3 256 q55 p10..13 TU0 -> IDENTICAL/TU6, kristenandsara
256 q55 p11..13 TU0 -> IDENTICAL, vidyo1 256 q55 p10 TU0 -> IDENTICAL,
plus johnny/vidyo4 rows moving to IDENTICAL at p10). Output pin moved:
photo-64x64-b8-p4-q25-f4-ld-Hybrid3115-Mainline 5554 -> 5577 B (non-base
frames at M4 correctly lost the tx-size rate term).

Acceptance at this commit: nextest 2756/2756; spotcheck 147/147;
video_key_matrix 75/75; pins 6/6 (regenerated, named cell);
identity_full_8bit 1100/1100; real_video_inter_gate 24/24;
